---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About | NM Nonprofits"
  description="NM Nonprofits is the definitive directory of New Mexico nonprofits, foundations, and grant opportunities."
>
  <div class="container-content py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">About NM Nonprofits</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg mb-12 leading-relaxed">
      The definitive directory of New Mexico's social sector, built to connect communities with the organizations that serve them.
    </p>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none space-y-10">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">What we are</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          NM Nonprofits is a comprehensive, searchable directory of nonprofit organizations, foundations, and funders operating in New Mexico. We index 501(c)(3) public charities, community foundations, tribal nonprofits, fiscal sponsors, and the philanthropic institutions that support them, across all 33 New Mexico counties.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Our goal is simple: make it easy to find the organizations doing the most important work in New Mexico, whether you are a donor, a grantseeker, a journalist, a researcher, or a community member looking for help.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          NM Nonprofits is an independent, privately owned directory and media platform. We are not a 501(c)(3) organization or affiliated with the state government.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Why we built this</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          New Mexico has over 7,000 registered nonprofits serving communities from Gallup to Roswell to the pueblos of the Rio Grande corridor. But finding the right organization, one that works in your region, serves your issue area, and is currently active, has historically required piecing together IRS databases, outdated county listings, and word-of-mouth referrals.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Funders face the same problem in reverse: identifying organizations doing strong work in specific regions or issue areas requires relationship networks that not every grantseeker has access to. NM Nonprofits was built to close that gap: one searchable, current, human-maintained directory that serves the whole New Mexico social sector.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">What we cover</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
          <li>3,000+ nonprofit organizations across all 33 New Mexico counties</li>
          <li>Community foundations, private foundations, and government funders</li>
          <li>Open and rolling grant opportunities for NM nonprofits and artists</li>
          <li>Sector-by-sector issue area browsing across 12 focus areas</li>
          <li>Five regional filters: Albuquerque Metro, Northern NM, Southern NM, Four Corners, and Eastern NM</li>
          <li>Nonprofit jobs in New Mexico</li>
          <li>Events, trainings, and professional development opportunities</li>
          <li>Tools, guides, databases, and resources for NM nonprofits and artists</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">How our data works</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Our directory is built from a combination of IRS Form 990 public records, New Mexico Secretary of State registration data, direct organization submissions, and editorial research. We review listings for accuracy and maintain descriptions that reflect each organization's current mission and programs.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Organizations can claim and update their own listing at any time. If information is out of date or incorrect, email us at <a href="mailto:corrections@nmnonprofits.com" class="text-turquoise-700 hover:underline">corrections@nmnonprofits.com</a> and we will update it promptly. Our goal is a living directory, not a static snapshot.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Our focus on arts and culture</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          New Mexico has one of the most distinctive arts economies in the United States. Santa Fe is among the top three art markets in the country. Taos has sustained a working artist community for over a century. Indigenous arts traditions, Hispano folk arts, and contemporary studio practice exist side by side across the state. NM Nonprofits gives particular attention to arts and culture organizations, arts funders, and grants available to artists, including resources on fiscal sponsorship, arts grant applications, and the creative economy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Get listed</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Basic listings are free. If your organization is not in the directory yet, submit it through our listing form. Premium tiers offer enhanced visibility, featured placement, and a more detailed profile page.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <a href="/submit/" class="btn-primary">Submit Your Organization</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">Contact us</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          Questions, corrections, or partnership inquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@nmnonprofits.com" class="text-turquoise-700 hover:underline">hello@nmnonprofits.com</a>. For listing corrections: <a href="mailto:corrections@nmnonprofits.com" class="text-turquoise-700 hover:underline">corrections@nmnonprofits.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- Founder section -->
    <div class="mt-20 pt-12 border-t border-gray-100">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-10">About the Founder</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-8 items-start">

        <div class="flex-shrink-0">
          <div class="w-36 h-36 rounded-full overflow-hidden">
            <img src="/images/founder.jpg" alt="M.G. Salazar at the Tribeca Film Festival" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-serif font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">M.G. Salazar</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-turquoise-700 font-medium mb-4">Founder</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            M.G. Salazar is a two-time Creative Arts Emmy Award winner, author, and grant-winning multidisciplinary artist with roots in New Mexico. Trained in nonprofit management at NYU and the founder of La Resistencia Press, M.G. built NM Nonprofits out of a direct experience with how hard it can be to find the organizations doing the most important work in this state. The directory is designed to change that.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 italic mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            Built by someone from here, for everyone doing the work here.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
